\@writefile{lof}{\defcounter {refsection}{0}\relax }\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces  Proposed framework for the design problem of programmable collective behavior in microrobot swarms. \textit  {Microrobot physics} describes the physical mechanisms governing individual robots (e.g., acoustic streaming, magnetic interactions, and Brownian motion). \textit  {Behavioral rules} describes local control decisions executed in response to neighboring robots or the environment. \textit  {Collective behavior} describes the emergent swarm dynamics (e.g., toroids, swarming) arising from local interactions. The forward problem predicts collective behavior from the underlying robot physics, while the inverse-design problem seeks to determine the microrobot physics required to realize a desired collective behavior. \relax }}{1}{}\protected@file@percent }
